<section class="section wrap closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
  <h2 class="closing-title" id="closing-title">
    We don't need people to read more code. We need a system where nobody has to pretend they did.
  </h2>

  <div class="closing-grid">
    <div class="prose">
      <h3 class="subhead">Why “Onus”</h3>
      <p>
        From <i>onus probandi</i>, the burden of proof. Today it sits on a reviewer who has to find what's wrong
        by reading lines. Onus moves it to the agent, which has to show its work. It shouldn't matter whose
        agents do that work; what matters is what they can prove.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        Onus puts into practice the Agentic Coding Paradigm, set out by Mikias Abebe in the manifesto{" "}
        <i>Code Is Not the Product</i> (September 2026).
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/onushq">Follow Onus on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer class="site-footer wrap" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
  <h2 class="subhead" id="sources-title">Sources</h2>
  <ol class="sources">
    {
      sources.map((s, i) => (
        <li id={`source-${i + 1}`}>
          <a href={s.url}>{s.title}</a>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
  <p class="fine">© 2026 Onus</p>
</footer>

